# WK-Hub BitLocker PIN

# ── Packaging output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The .intunewin is a build artefact — rebuild it from Source\ rather than
# committing it, so what you upload always matches the scripts in this repo.
Output/
*.intunewin

# ── Microsoft tools you supply yourself ─────────────────────────────────────
# Neither is redistributed with this product. Download them from Microsoft:
#   IntuneWinAppUtil.exe — Win32 Content Prep Tool
#   ServiceUI.exe        — Microsoft Deployment Toolkit
# Ignored here so a local copy is never committed by accident.
IntuneWinAppUtil.exe
ServiceUI.exe

# ── Runtime / test output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Install, uninstall and prompt logs can name devices and users.
*.log
prompt.log
_testrun/
_sandbox/

# ── Optional branding you drop in ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The PIN dialog degrades to a text wordmark when these are absent, so your own
# artwork stays yours and is not committed by mistake. Delete these two lines if
# you would rather track your branding in your fork.
brand-*.png
*-logo-*.png

# ...except the reference artwork under docs/. Those three PNGs are dimensions
# and format, not anyone's brand, and BRANDING.md tells adopters to copy them.
!docs/branding-sample/
!docs/branding-sample/*.png

# ── Editor / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
